    <briefdescription>
<para>Bytes of one source behind one view: a mapped file, a buffer read into memory, or a supplied text. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="class_input" kindref="compound">Input</ref> owns each mapping and each buffer that it creates. The standard-input mapping is held by native, which unmaps it when the <ref refid="class_input" kindref="compound">Input</ref> is destroyed. A mapped file is held by mappedFile, which unmaps it. A buffer is held by buffer. A supplied text is not owned, so the view refers to the caller&apos;s text. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
